flowchart TD
  IN["<b>Inputs</b><br/>your file (Excel, CSV or PDF) · your scorecard · optional source documents"]

  F["<b>1 · Freeze</b><br/>read once · lock the file and the scorecard with a fingerprint (hash)<br/>make sure three different AI families are set up<br/>check every sheet the scorecard names exists"]

  C["<b>2 · Count in code</b><br/>exact counts give a pass share per question<br/>the share turns into a 0-5 mark"]

  R["<b>3 · Examiners 1, 2, 3 mark</b>  on their own, at the same time<br/>same instructions · 0-5 per question · each mark points at a cell"]

  EV{"Does the mark point at a real cell?<br/>sheet and cell exist<br/>quote really in the cell"}
  DISC["Set the claim aside<br/>(recorded in the report)"]

  K["<b>4 · Final reviewer</b>  compares the three sets of marks<br/>merges repeated issues"]

  RULES["Code applies the rules<br/>the mark stays inside the Examiners' range<br/>a gap over 1 point needs evidence from the file<br/>otherwise the lower mark stands"]

  D["<b>5 · Decide by a fixed rule</b><br/>weighted score out of 100<br/>below 60 red · 60-74 amber · 75+ green"]

  OUT{"Verdict"}
  GRN["GREEN<br/>75 or more"]
  AMB["AMBER<br/>60 to 74"]
  RED["RED<br/>below 60"]

  REPT["<b>6 · Report</b><br/>what to fix first · path to green · charts<br/>PDF, Excel and Markdown · full record kept"]

  FREEZE2["Check the file again<br/>stop if it changed mid-run"]

  IN --> F --> C --> R --> EV
  EV -- no --> DISC --> K
  EV -- yes --> K
  K --> RULES --> D --> OUT
  OUT --> GRN
  OUT --> AMB
  OUT --> RED
  GRN --> FREEZE2
  AMB --> FREEZE2
  RED --> FREEZE2
  FREEZE2 --> REPT

  classDef step fill:#0f2a27,stroke:#2dd4bf,color:#ececf0
  classDef gate fill:#14141a,stroke:#7aa2f7,color:#ececf0
  classDef good fill:#0f2218,stroke:#3ecf8e,color:#ececf0
  classDef warn fill:#262010,stroke:#f5b13d,color:#ececf0
  classDef bad fill:#2a1413,stroke:#f2655c,color:#ececf0
  class F,C,R,K,D,REPT step
  class EV,OUT gate
  class GRN good
  class AMB warn
  class RED,DISC bad
